health: charging limit through Motorola's IMotoHealth HAL

Project: lineage-sdk (LineageOS lineage-24.0)

LineageOS's charging control (Settings > Battery > Charging control) needs the
vendor.lineage.health IChargingControl HAL, which a stock Motorola vendor does not have, so on
this generic system image the Lineage health service never started and the page was hidden.

The stock vendor has its own HAL for the same job: motorola.hardware.health.IMotoHealth/default
(AIDL V3). Its setChgLimits(lower, upper) writes the kernel's adaptive-charge thresholds
(/sys/module/qpnp_adaptive_charge/parameters/{lower,upper}_limit): charging stops at "upper" and
starts again at "lower". Stock Android 17 calls it from system_server (BatteryService), and the
stock vendor SELinux policy makes system_server a client of that HAL, so no policy change is
needed. Method order, transaction codes and argument order were read from the stock
framework's generated proxy (services.jar), the accepted range from the vendor service
(upper 1..100, lower below upper, negative upper = off).

ChargingControlController falls back to a small adapter (MotoChargingControl) when the Lineage
HAL is not declared. It offers LIMIT mode only, which LineageOS's Limit provider drives with the
selected percentage and its recharge margin. "No limit" (100 %) is sent as off (-1, -1), not as
a 100 % threshold, which would only resume charging at 0 %. Devices with the Lineage HAL are
unaffected: the fallback runs only when that HAL is absent.

Limit provider: with a HAL that offers LIMIT but not DEADLINE, the controller also uses the
Limit provider for the Auto and Custom schedule modes, but the provider only implemented the
percentage callback; the base class's time-based callback throws, in system_server, as soon as
such a schedule is active while the phone charges. It now implements that callback: inside the
scheduled window the battery is held at 80 %, and the limit is lifted early enough to reach
100 % at the target time (Android's time-to-full estimate taken near the hold level, one hour
if there is none, plus config_chargingControlTimeMargin).

